WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.190
If you've been down in the dumps ever since
it was revealed that the upcoming sixth season

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:08.080
of History's drama series Vikings would be
its last, it's time to pick yourself back

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.080
up.

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.160
A new Vikings spin-off series has been announced,
and soon Vikings: Valhalla will be streaming

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.240
on Netflix.

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.610
But first, a warning: Spoilers for Vikings
ahead!

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:21.060
Before you start scrolling through Netflix's
thousands of offerings looking for Valhalla,

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:25.130
know this: No release date has yet been announced
for the series.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:29.760
Considering that the show's existence was
only confirmed in November 2019, Netflix is

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.810
likely nowhere near announcing a start date
for the series.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:35.150
For comparison, just take a look at The Witcher.

00:00:35.150 --> 00:00:40.090
That show was first announced way back in
May 2017, but it wasn't until Halloween of

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:43.900
2019 - two-and-a-half years later - that Netflix
announced the release date.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:48.720
That debut date, by the way, was December
20, 2019 - meaning it wasn't announced until

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.070
less than two months before the premiere.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.570
While Vikings: Valhalla may not have quite
as long of a wait given that it's spinning

00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:58.540
off from a property instead of building one
from the ground up, there's no reason to believe

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:02.240
that Netflix will announce a release date
for the show anytime soon.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.330
It's also worth mentioning that, since Vikings:
Valhalla is meant to be a follow-up to Vikings,

00:01:06.330 --> 00:01:09.360
fans won't see it until after the original
series ends.

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:13.100
But forget about the question of when you'll
see it; a better question is, what exactly

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:14.940
is this spinoff going to be about?

00:01:14.940 --> 00:01:18.780
If there's one thing that Vikings has been
great at doing, it's killing off its main

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.040
characters.

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.600
Season 3 saw the deaths of Earl Haraldson's
widow Siggy and the priest Athelstan.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.270
Vikings season 4 knocked off Ragnar's second
wife Aslaug, his friend and rival King Ecbert,

00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:33.340
and most shockingly of all, Ragnar himself,
who up until that point had been the series'

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:34.340
main protagonist.

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.610
"Your father was a great hero.

00:01:36.610 --> 00:01:39.920
Perhaps the greatest hero of our race.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:42.930
And that is why we have answered your summons.”

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:47.180
As more characters were added in season 5,
the bodies continued to pile up, with seemingly

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.520
no character being safe from week to week.

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:53.320
By the time Vikings concludes its run, it's
possible that there won't even be any main

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:56.909
Vikings cast members left alive to return
for Valhalla.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:01:58.780
And frankly, fans shouldn't expect there to
be.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:02.710
It has been confirmed that the new series
will take place around 100 years after the

00:02:02.710 --> 00:02:07.070
current show, meaning that even the youngest
Vikings characters will be dead and gone by

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:08.070
then.

00:02:08.070 --> 00:02:12.110
Instead, Vikings: Valhalla will feature all-new
characters based on even more historical figures

00:02:12.110 --> 00:02:13.590
from Norse legend.

00:02:13.590 --> 00:02:17.230
Some of the main characters of the new series
will reportedly be such legendary figures

00:02:17.230 --> 00:02:20.860
as Leif Erikson, Harald Hardrada, William
the Conqueror, and more.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:25.340
Even though the 100-year time gap will make
things tricky, Alexander Ludwig has suggested

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.370
that his character, Bjorn Ironside, may not
have finished his Vikings journey.

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:32.790
Whether that means some kind of flashback
sequence on the new spin-off series or an

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:35.930
appearance in a potential feature film remains
to be seen.

00:02:35.930 --> 00:02:40.450
It's just nice to know Ludwig isn't quite
ready to leave the world of Vikings behind.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:44.280
Since the spin-off was announced only recently,
plot details have been scarce.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:48.379
But that doesn't mean we can't make a few
educated guesses as to what kinds of stories

00:02:48.379 --> 00:02:52.340
Vikings: Valhalla will be looking to tell,
since we know a few of the main characters.

00:02:52.340 --> 00:02:55.319
And to do that, we'll look to real Viking
history.

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:58.480
Leif Erikson is arguably the most famous of
the lot.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.250
He has a pretty big claim to fame, as he's
believed to be the first European to discover

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:05.650
North America - rather than that imposter
Christopher Columbus.

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.200
"You're a phony!

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.230
Hey everybody!

00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:11.340
This guy's a great, big phony!"

00:03:11.340 --> 00:03:15.030
Not only that, but Leif Erikson is said to
have done so a whole half-millennium before

00:03:15.030 --> 00:03:19.030
Columbus sailed the ocean blue, setting foot
in a land he dubbed "Vinland" back in the

00:03:19.030 --> 00:03:20.489
11th century.

00:03:20.489 --> 00:03:22.120
Next is Harald Hardrada.

00:03:22.120 --> 00:03:27.239
Born about 45 years after Leif Erikson, he's
regarded as the last great Viking King, having

00:03:27.239 --> 00:03:31.430
fought for control of Norway and Denmark before
meeting his end during an invasion of England.

00:03:31.430 --> 00:03:36.739
His successor, in some respects, was his contemporary
- the Norman King William the Conqueror, who

00:03:36.739 --> 00:03:41.310
wasn't a Viking but claimed Viking ancestry
as a descendent of the one-and-only Rollo.

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.530
William conquered England following Harald
Hardrada's defeat, becoming its king.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:49.440
The pair's respective battles will almost
certainly factor into the plot of Vikings:

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:50.360
Valhalla.

